From 3a26c240eaaafe9eefbfdee1650acdc5926bb1ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 14:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] ktranslate: implement CDP neighbor walk

Fills in pollCDPNeighbors / parseCDPNeighbors to walk cdpCacheEntry
(1.3.6.1.4.1.9.9.23.1.2.1.1) and translate the columns we care about
(device id, device port, platform, address, capabilities) into
kt.TopologyNeighbor records. The local ifIndex comes directly from the
cdpCacheEntry index, and LocalIfName is filled in from the interface
metadata already collected earlier in the poll cycle.

The walker/parser split keeps the OID-decoding logic pure so it can be
exercised by synthetic PDUs; unit tests cover two-neighbor walks, nil
ifaces fallback, OID suffix splitting, and protocol selection.
---
